  "taskCall": {
    "context": "# Goal\nKengaku lane, round 67: ONE v1 wave of 13 seats (build + attack). You are ONE seat of this wave. The round's two claims are FROZEN in /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kengaku-shokunin/plans/round-67-claims.md (read it first, in full; commit dcc39ea3). Predicates, counters, kill rules, the frozen six-case vector table and the frontier quotes are fixed there. No seat changes them. A seat that thinks a rule is wrong reports it in its output and does not edit it.\n\n# Paths (absolute; every Report: trailer is relative to /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kengaku-shokunin; write it at /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kengaku-shokunin/<that path>)\n- L = /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kengaku-shokunin (lane repo). Write NOTHING in L except where your item names a path. Seats write only into their own seat dir.\n- W = /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kengaku-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-67/w1 (wave evidence). Your seat dir is W/<your seat name>/ (mkdir -p).\n- S = /fast/scratch/hyaku/kengaku-r67 (scratch root). Your scratch dir is S/<your seat name>/ (mkdir -p). Pass it explicitly: TMPDIR=S/<seat>, --work S/<seat>. Never build under /tmp; /tmp is for files under 50 MB only.\n- Pipeline venv (read-only for you, never modify, never install into it): /home/vgpnk/.local/share/kengaku-r67/venv-pipe (python 3.14.8, torch 2.15.0+cpu, transformers 5.22.1, pytest 9.2.0).\n- Port lock: /home/vgpnk/.local/share/kengaku-r67/port-12355.lock. Every run of the grader (any pytest of test_outputs.py, any probe run that starts a gloo listener on 127.0.0.1:12355) MUST be wrapped as `flock /home/vgpnk/.local/share/kengaku-r67/port-12355.lock <command>`. The probe takes that lock itself; you add the wrap only for your own grader runs. Never start your own listener on 12355.\n- Probe (frozen, read-only for you): /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kengaku-shokunin/plans/round67_c1_pipeline_probe.py. Committed receipt of record (read-only): /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kengaku-shokunin/corpus/evidence/round67/pipe/receipt.txt, junit beside it in receipt.junit/. Committed cases (read-only): /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kengaku-shokunin/corpus/evidence/round67/pipe/cases/<case>/pipeline_parallel.py. Grader capture (read-only): /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kengaku-shokunin/corpus/evidence/round52/graders/torch-pipeline-parallelism/tests/test_outputs.py (sha256 23574246a407163a8e6581c84287cc2f1eb745efbaad2a317a5a28c39958c64f). Live source captures (read-only): corpus/evidence/round67/sources/.\n- Committed R65 sqlite probe and receipt (read-only): /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kengaku-shokunin/plans/round65_c1_sqlite_probe.py and /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kengaku-shokunin/corpus/evidence/round65/sqlite-gcov-probe.txt. Fabricated fixture (read-only): /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kengaku-shokunin/corpus/evidence/round66/red/fabricated-r65.txt.\n\n# Contract\n- Scratch discipline: a trap 'rm -rf -- \"$S\"' EXIT (shell) or finally: shutil.rmtree (Python) removes your scratch dir before you yield; copy every receipt you cite into your seat dir first. The driver reaps scratch with no live process and no file change for 45 minutes.\n- Network: only (a) https://raw.githubusercontent.com/harbor-framework/terminal-bench-2/2fd12b88aafdd04a52c298e3940bcb189f9766d6/... and (b) https://sqlite.org/... . No other network. No PyPI and no download.pytorch.org. No credentials: never read ~/.ssh, ~/.config/gh, ~/.netrc, ~/.omp secrets, or any op:// reference.\n- Git: never run git add, commit, stash, checkout, switch, reset, pull, push or fetch, and no mutating jj command, anywhere. Read-only git (show, log, ls-files, rev-parse, cat-file, diff, status, merge-base, grep) is fine, using git -C /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kengaku-shokunin.\n- Never edit MANIFEST.json, the fleet root, .ufo/state/, .ufo/watchdog.log, /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokuknow (read-only: run nothing there), any sibling lane, or .scratch/. Never edit the frozen files in L (plans/round67_c1_pipeline_probe.py, plans/round-67-claims.md, corpus/evidence/round67/**, corpus/SOURCES.md, corpus/evidence/round65/**, plans/round65_c1_sqlite_probe.py).\n- Never pass a model. Do not use the ask tool. Do not poll: the only waits allowed are those your item names (at most 20 checks, sleep 60 between checks).\n- Every observed value carries the command that produced it. An unrun check has not passed. A receipt you cite must be a file you actually wrote with observed bytes.\n- Yield a terminal result: the file paths you wrote and at most 15 key lines with verdicts.\n\n# Tooling sentence\nTooling authorization (operator, 2026-10-19): you and every seat may install or upgrade tools that help the task; first read /home/vgpnk/.omp/agent/RULES.md; record tool, version, channel, reason. pacman is PAUSED host-wide: install via uv tool, npx or an official binary in ~/.local/bin, never pacman. Never run pacman -S, -Sy, -Syu, -U or -R.\n\n# Frozen facts (L1 measured pre-freeze; receipts committed)\n- Host: Arch Linux; python 3.14.8 (/usr/bin/python3); bwrap 0.13.1 (/usr/bin/bwrap); uv 0.13.0; gcc/gcov 16.2.1; host sqlite3 at /usr/bin/sqlite3; 32 cores.\n- Receipt of record: corpus/evidence/round67/pipe/receipt.txt (six VECTOR lines: q1-ref PPPP; q2-none FFFF; q3-stub PPFF; q4-hooks-noop PFPP; q5-full-model PPPF; q6-unscaled-loss PPFF; vector order exists/no_hooks/ws1/ws2).\n- Claims in brief: R67-C1 (coverage, L0-capped; capability offline-torch-pipeline-parallel-grader-probe): predicate `python3 plans/round67_c1_pipeline_probe.py --check-receipt corpus/evidence/round67/pipe/receipt.txt` prints PREDICATE R67-C1 pass. R67-C2 (operability, held at ceiling 10): the committed R65 sqlite checker gains a --strict mode (clauses s1-s6 in the claims doc) that exits 1 on the fabricated fixture and 0 on the committed R65 receipt; default mode output unchanged.\n- L0 questions carried, nothing assumed answered: kengaku | round-25/33/51 (coverage cap), round-56, round-63, round-54 (assimilation id drift; assimilation none this round).\n\n# Tooling-only rule\nInstall nothing unless your item names it. Any install is recorded as tool, version, channel, reason in your output.\n\n# Output\nWrite your seat's files under W/<seat>/ and yield the terminal result: paths written, at most 15 key lines with verdicts, and the exact commands you ran with exit codes.",
    "tasks": [
      {
        "name": "TensorRecon",
        "agent": "scout",
        "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\nRead-only audit of the frozen R67-C1 vector table against the grader. No edits anywhere; no grader run.\n1. Read plans/round-67-claims.md (R67-C1 section only) and plans/round67_c1_pipeline_probe.py (FROZEN_TABLE, KEYS, key_of, check_receipt).\n2. Read the grader corpus/evidence/round52/graders/torch-pipeline-parallelism/tests/test_outputs.py in full (it is about 180 lines).\n3. For each of q1-ref, q2-none, q3-stub, q4-hooks-noop, q5-full-model, q6-unscaled-loss, and each of the four legs exists, no_hooks, ws1, ws2: state with grader line numbers and the case file's lines whether the frozen P or F follows from the assertions. Treat the world_size 2 layer-count assertion at line 144 and the mp.spawn failure path as part of the derivation.\n4. Flag any frozen value you cannot derive, and any leg whose outcome depends on hang, timeout, or barrier behaviour.\n5. Write W/TensorRecon/recon.md with one row per case x leg: expected P/F, derivation with line numbers, confidence (derived / inferred). Yield the summary.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch.\nJudged on: coverage, operability, calibration\nMilestone: kengaku r67 w1 (v1, 13 seats: build + attack): R67-C1 offline torch-pipeline-parallel grader probe (coverage, L0-capped); R67-C2 round-65 sqlite receipt gate strict mode (operability); frontier knowledge and lesson drafts; source re-read\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-67/w1/TensorRecon.md"
      },
      {
        "name": "CaseAudit",
        "agent": "reviewer",
        "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\nSurgical correctness review of the six case files. Read-only; no edits; no grader run.\n1. Read each of corpus/evidence/round67/pipe/cases/{q1-ref,q3-stub,q4-hooks-noop,q5-full-model,q6-unscaled-loss}/pipeline_parallel.py in full. q2-none has no file by design.\n2. For each file, confirm it matches its description in plans/round-67-claims.md (q1 correct AFAB with partition, blocking send/recv and all forwards before backwards; q3 stub that raises; q4 q1 schedule plus a no-op forward hook whose literal register_forward_hook appears in code; q5 no partition with every rank running every layer; q6 q1 schedule with the loss not divided by the microbatch count).\n3. Run sha256sum on each committed file and check it against the case_sha256 in corpus/evidence/round67/pipe/receipt.txt (grep '^CASE'). Record each match or mismatch with the command output.\n4. Name any defect that would make a case's observed vector differ from the frozen table for a reason other than the grader's assertions (for example a file that cannot import, a syntax error, a hidden side effect, a reliance on /tmp).\n5. Write W/CaseAudit/audit.md. Yield the summary with each case's verdict.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch.\nJudged on: coverage, operability, calibration\nMilestone: kengaku r67 w1 (v1, 13 seats: build + attack): R67-C1 offline torch-pipeline-parallel grader probe (coverage, L0-capped); R67-C2 round-65 sqlite receipt gate strict mode (operability); frontier knowledge and lesson drafts; source re-read\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-67/w1/CaseAudit.md"
      },
      {
        "name": "ProbeReview",
        "agent": "reviewer",
        "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\nSurgical correctness review of the frozen R67-C1 probe. Read-only; no edits; no grader run.\n1. Read plans/round67_c1_pipeline_probe.py in full.\n2. Compare its predicate and receipt label with the single predicate sentence in plans/round-67-claims.md (R67-C1 Predicate). The sentence, the code's check_receipt, and the receipt label must name the same conditions. List each mismatch with line numbers.\n3. Check the bwrap argv in run_case: network and PID unshare, read-only binds of /usr, /etc, venv, case and grader, /tmp as tmpfs, clearenv, and that nothing writes under /tmp. Check the flock and port-busy ordering, and the handling of a timeout (must exit 2, never a verdict).\n4. Check that check_receipt re-derives the junit outcomes from receipt.junit/<case>.xml and compares them with the VECTOR line; check the handling of a missing case, a duplicate CASE line and a malformed line (named findings, never a traceback).\n5. Run `python3 -m py_compile plans/round67_c1_pipeline_probe.py` with PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 and `python3 plans/round67_c1_pipeline_probe.py --check-receipt corpus/evidence/round67/pipe/receipt.txt; echo rc=$?`, and record both outputs. The --check-receipt run reads only committed bytes.\n6. Write W/ProbeReview/review.md with findings ranked by severity (must-fix, should-fix, nit), each with a line number and a one-line fix suggestion routed to the lane. Yield the summary.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch.\nJudged on: coverage, operability, calibration\nMilestone: kengaku r67 w1 (v1, 13 seats: build + attack): R67-C1 offline torch-pipeline-parallel grader probe (coverage, L0-capped); R67-C2 round-65 sqlite receipt gate strict mode (operability); frontier knowledge and lesson drafts; source re-read\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-67/w1/ProbeReview.md"
      },
      {
        "name": "SourceReview",
        "agent": "reviewer",
        "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\nSecond-seat re-read of the two new registry rows (Q10). Read-only on L; network allowed only for the two pinned URLs.\n1. Read corpus/SOURCES.md rows S238 and S239 (grep -n '^| S23[89]' corpus/SOURCES.md).\n2. Re-fetch the two pinned URLs into your scratch dir with curl -s -m 30 and record the HTTP status and sha256sum of each. Compare the sha256 of the grader with corpus/evidence/round52/graders/SHA256SUMS line 169 and the sha256 of the instruction with the value 989bfcf0c54baf6c8cdc391743dbb2f9e858c5779dd85112536875d4d1b2dcd2.\n3. For each quote and line number the rows cite (S238: :154-157 verbatim 'AFAB violation: found forward after backward at {key}', def test_no_hooks_in_pipeline_parallel at :31, exists at :19, parametrised world sizes at :171-172; S239: :18 verbatim 'Run forward passes for all microbatches first, then run backward passes.' and :31 'You must not use hooks inside your implementation.'), run grep -n against the capture file in corpus/evidence/round67/sources/ and record the result. A quote must match verbatim; a line must contain it.\n4. Check the row's word count for each quote (25 words or fewer) and that the status and recheck cells are well-formed.\n5. Write W/SourceReview/source-review.md with one verdict per row (pass or the specific defect) and the commands with their output. Yield the summary.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch.\nJudged on: coverage, operability, calibration\nMilestone: kengaku r67 w1 (v1, 13 seats: build + attack): R67-C1 offline torch-pipeline-parallel grader probe (coverage, L0-capped); R67-C2 round-65 sqlite receipt gate strict mode (operability); frontier knowledge and lesson drafts; source re-read\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-67/w1/SourceReview.md"
      },
      {
        "name": "ProbeMutate",
        "agent": "mutation-tester",
        "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\nMutate-run-revert probe for the R67-C1 receipt checker. No port use, no grader run. Work only in your scratch dir.\n1. Copy corpus/evidence/round67/pipe/receipt.txt and the directory receipt.junit/ into S/ProbeMutate/base/ (keep the directory name receipt.junit beside a receipt file named receipt.txt).\n2. Create at least eight mutated receipts in S/ProbeMutate/mut/ (each a copy of base with one change): flip one VECTOR character for one case; delete one VECTOR line; delete one CASE line; change one case_sha256 to 64 zeros; change one junit_sha256 to 64 zeros; change the PROBE sha to 64 zeros; change the PROBE version token; change the GRADER sha; change a frozen-table row by editing the VECTOR line for q5-full-model to PPPP; delete the PREDICATE-relevant receipt.junit file for q3-stub (copy the directory then remove the one file).\n3. Run `python3 plans/round67_c1_pipeline_probe.py --check-receipt <mutant>` from L with PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 for each mutant, and for the unmodified base copy. Record rc for each. The base must give rc 0. Each mutant must give rc 1 with a CHECK defect finding and must not produce a traceback; a traceback counts as a must-fix finding.\n4. Revert is by deleting the mutant directory, never by editing the committed receipt.\n5. Write W/ProbeMutate/mutations.md: a table of mutant, expected rc 1, observed rc, finding text. Yield the summary with the count of mutants killed.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch.\nJudged on: coverage, operability, calibration\nMilestone: kengaku r67 w1 (v1, 13 seats: build + attack): R67-C1 offline torch-pipeline-parallel grader probe (coverage, L0-capped); R67-C2 round-65 sqlite receipt gate strict mode (operability); frontier knowledge and lesson drafts; source re-read\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-67/w1/ProbeMutate.md"
      },
      {
        "name": "ReceiptMutate",
        "agent": "mutation-tester",
        "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\nBuild the mutation corpus for the R67-C2 strict gate and its runner. Do not edit any lane file. Do not run the strict mode (the proposal is built by another seat); you prepare fixtures and a runner that the lead runs after the proposal lands.\n1. Copy the committed R65 receipt corpus/evidence/round65/sqlite-gcov-probe.txt into S/ReceiptMutate/base.txt and the fabricated fixture corpus/evidence/round66/red/fabricated-r65.txt into S/ReceiptMutate/fab.txt.\n2. Write W/ReceiptMutate/fixtures/ with one file per mutation, each derived from base.txt by one change, for these clauses of plans/round-67-claims.md R67-C2: s1 (remove the instrument header line; change its version token to r65-c1/9); s2 (change the GRADER sha to 64 zeros); s3 (change the AMALG sha to 64 zeros); s4 (change the TOOLCHAIN gcc value to 15.0.0); s5 (change one RUN line's rc to 1; change one RUN line's driver to fabricated; delete one NOBIND line); s6 (change one VECTOR line for G3 to P/P/P). Name each file m-s<clause>-<n>.txt. Expected strict verdict for each: exit 1 with a CHECK defect finding naming that clause.\n3. Write W/ReceiptMutate/fixtures/expected.tsv with columns file, clause, expected_rc (1). Include base.txt with expected_rc 0 and fab.txt with expected_rc 1.\n4. Write W/ReceiptMutate/run_strict_fixtures.sh: a POSIX shell script that takes one argument (the path to the strict-capable checker), loops over expected.tsv, runs `python3 <checker> --check-receipt <fixture> --strict`, and fails with a nonzero exit if any observed rc differs from expected_rc. The script must not use /tmp and must not touch the lane. Do not run it against any checker that does not exist yet.\n5. Verify the script's own syntax with `sh -n W/ReceiptMutate/run_strict_fixtures.sh` and record the output.\n6. Write W/ReceiptMutate/report.md listing each fixture, its clause, and the expected verdict, plus the note that the lead runs the script after the proposal lands. Yield the summary.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch.\nJudged on: coverage, operability, calibration\nMilestone: kengaku r67 w1 (v1, 13 seats: build + attack): R67-C1 offline torch-pipeline-parallel grader probe (coverage, L0-capped); R67-C2 round-65 sqlite receipt gate strict mode (operability); frontier knowledge and lesson drafts; source re-read\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-67/w1/ReceiptMutate.md"
      },
      {
        "name": "StrictGateBuild",
        "agent": "executor",
